s " [:a {:href "/athletes/78360"} "Earl Eby"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The semi-finals and final of this event were held only 30 minutes apart.  In the final, Eby and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79008"} "Don Scott"] " (USA) led for the first lap, with Eby passing 400 in 54.2.  Bevil Rudd took the lead with a lap remaining and held it until the final straight.  He faded in the stretch, as Hill and Eby fought out a close finish, with Hill pulling ahead in the last few metres.  Hill had first come to prominence in 1909, finishing fourth in AAA four-mile event.  During the war, he served as a signalman in the Royal Flying Corps.  Earl Eby later became one of America’s top track writers."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "398"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69148"} "Albert Hill"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "1:56.2est / at 8 metres (2 h2)"] [:td {} "1:56.4 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "1:53.4 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "160"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78360"} "Earl Eby"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:56.8est / at 5 metres (3 h2)"] [:td {} "1:57.0est / at 4 metres (2 h3)"] [:td {} "1:53.6 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "561"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75317"} "Bevil Rudd"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right